    },
    {
      "id": "nqAdYofp4tckFH-dEDcyA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 453.07948792299595,
      "y": 549.1538578087951,
      "width": 578.879150390625,
      "height": 351,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 527285683,
      "version": 765,
      "versionNonce": 906434579,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790945846701,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "<I like mostly how you described kNN. \nBut besides standard kNN hyperparameters we also added \nas options retry mechanism, and using neighbours whose \nactions are relatively close. We have to describe this.\nLet's not talk about specific VLAs here, just mention we can use \nVLAs internal state as embedder. And we can do it before and \nafter finetuning. And I don't really like your graph at the bottom.\nI think maybe some visualiazation with optuna trials with \nmost import hyperparameters would be nicer. Optuna \nhas nice plotly visualizations. Also btw maybe we do more than \n50 trials of optuna.>\n\nSo here everything person need to now how our kNN works.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "<I like mostly how you described kNN. \nBut besides standard kNN hyperparameters we also added \nas options retry mechanism, and using neighbours whose \nactions are relatively close. We have to describe this.\nLet's not talk about specific VLAs here, just mention we can use \nVLAs internal state as embedder. And we can do it before and \nafter finetuning. And I don't really like your graph at the bottom.\nI think maybe some visualiazation with optuna trials with \nmost import hyperparameters would be nicer. Optuna \nhas nice plotly visualizations. Also btw maybe we do more than \n50 trials of optuna.>\n\nSo here everything person need to now how our kNN works.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
